-[0m[32mThe deeper point is about personal responsibility and freedom. Medical professionals shouldn't be forced to violate their moral convictions to keep their licenses. Simultaneously, the medical profession has an obligation to ensure patient access through referral networks and professional networks. This is a balance—protecting conscience rights while ensuring care continuity. Communities work through these logistics in various ways: some physicians refer to colleagues, others ensure geographic access, and some regions develop networks of willing providers.
-[0m[32m
