-[0m[32mAbsolutely. Title IX's core mission is protecting students from discrimination and harassment based on sex, and we now understand that includes gender identity and sexual orientation. Without specific guidance on deadnaming and misgendering, we're leaving transgender and non-binary students vulnerable to psychological harm and hostile learning environments. These practices constitute harassment that directly interferes with educational access. When schools have clear policies protecting students from intentional misgendering and deadnaming, we see improved mental health outcomes, better attendance, and greater academic success. It's not about restricting speech—it's about ensuring all students, particularly our most vulnerable, can learn in safe, inclusive environments. This is a matter of basic human dignity and educational equity.<|im_end|>[0m[33m
