-[0m[32mThis is precisely why we need universal healthcare that treats gender-affirming care as the essential medical care it is. Every person—regardless of income—deserves access to the treatments they need to live authentically and healthily. We should be expanding Medicaid coverage, ensuring private plans cover these services without discriminatory exclusions, and moving toward a system where healthcare is a right, not a commodity. The current patchwork approach perpetuates inequality and harm.<|im_end|>[0m[33m
